-- Counting by fibres: a finite set is the sum of the sizes of the preimages
-- of a function on it, sums of constant and bounded weights, the
-- generalized pigeonhole principle, and the size of a disjoint union of a
-- finite family
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
